.Dd October 29, 2026
.Dt SIZE 1
.Os
.Sh NAME
.Nm size
.Nd show the sizes of the sections of object files
.Sh SYNOPSIS
.Nm
.Op Fl A | B | m
.Op Fl d | o | x
.Op Fl t
.Op Fl l
.Op Fl -arch Ns = Ns Ar arch
.Op Ar file ...
.Sh DESCRIPTION
.Nm
shows the size of the text, data and other sections of each object
file, archive member or executable, or of
.Pa a.out
when no
.Ar file
is given.
.Bl -tag -width Ds
.It Fl A , Fl -format Ns = Ns Cm sysv
One line per section, with its size and address.
.It Fl B , Fl -format Ns = Ns Cm berkeley
One line per file: text, data, bss, total in decimal and in hexadecimal
(the default).
.It Fl m , Fl -format Ns = Ns Cm darwin
Mach-O segments and their sections.
.It Fl l
With
.Fl m ,
show the addresses and offsets too.
.It Fl d , o , x
Show the sizes in decimal, octal or hexadecimal.
.It Fl t
Add a line with the totals (Berkeley format).
.It Fl -arch Ns = Ns Ar arch
Only the
.Ar arch
part of a universal file.
.El
.Sh EXIT STATUS
.Ex -std
.Sh SEE ALSO
.Xr ar 1 ,
.Xr strings 1
.Sh HISTORY
Minkar's
.Nm
is LLVM's llvm-size.
